<title>SRI LANKA: Tea Smallholder down on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Tea Smallholder down on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tea Smallholder Factories Ltd fell two percent, or 50 cents, to 24 rupees on turnover of 25,000 shares as small investors took profits, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a lot of profit to take in the stock which has moved up from about the 18-rupee level in the past few weeks,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>The company processes tea bought from small growers.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
